    name: 'The Gallows Dove',
    number: 30,
    realm: 'ash',
    glyph: '🕊',
    keywords: ['Peace', 'Execution'],
    upright: `I am the Gallows Dove. The peace in one of your rooms is false — everyone polite, nobody honest, the same unsaid thing sitting at every meal like a guest nobody invited. False peace is not the absence of war. It is war storing up interest. Let the performance die first: one true sentence, calmly said, about what is actually wrong. Real peace can only be built on that cleared ground — or the honest leaving that follows when peace is refused. Either way you win your life back. White feathers over a lie are still a lie.`,
    reversed: `In shadow, you either execute the wrong thing — the relationship, the friendship, your own hope — to end the discomfort quickly, or you clutch the fake harmony while it slowly poisons the well. Name the difference this week: what must end is the performance, not necessarily the people. Offer one honest peace term and watch what they do with it. Their answer is information you have been paying silence to avoid.`,
