    number: 33,
    realm: 'blood',
    glyph: '♛',
    keywords: ['Entanglement', 'Rule'],
    upright: `I am the Bramble Queen. Your life has thickets — obligations grown wild, relationships tangled past telling where yours ends and theirs begins, stories about yourself that were planted by other people's mouths. A thicket is not ruled by wishing. It is ruled by cutting corridors: one path cleared at a time, toward what you have chosen to crown. Some vines deserve the blade. Some deserve training onto a trellis, with limits they can climb. Know which is which by their fruit, not their familiarity. Entanglement marketed as love will call every pruning a betrayal. Prune anyway, Your Majesty.`,
    reversed: `Reversed, you either bleed on every thorn daily because cutting feels disloyal — or, in one scorched weekend, you burn the whole garden, loyal plants and all. Rule instead: one corridor this week. Crown one loyalty that has earned the crown. Cut one vine that only ever fed on you. A garden ruled a little at a time stays a garden. A garden abandoned belongs to the thorns.`,
