    upright: `I am the Pyre Scholar. You are in a curriculum nobody enrolls in on purpose: the burnout, the loss, the plan that burned in public. The realms keep no attendance records — but the lesson is real, and it is this: what survived the fire is your faculty, and what burned away was mostly costume. Study the burn like a scholar, not a victim. What did the flame reveal about your pace, your people, your pretending? Write the lesson down while the ash is still warm. Graduates of this school walk differently afterward: slower to flatter, quicker to leave bad rooms, impossible to sell the same illusion twice.`,
    reversed: `Reversed, you are collecting theories to avoid the heat — one more book, one more video, one more plan, anything but the applied exam — or you have started burning things just to feel the curriculum move. One lesson from the last fire, applied once, in a real situation, this week. That is the whole degree. Knowledge that has not survived contact with your actual life is decoration, and the pyre has no shelf for decorations.`,
