    reversed: `Reversed, every door feels like the last one — exhaustion making small choices feel fatal — or no door is ever allowed to be final, commitment dissolving into one more hallway of maybe. Rest if it is exhaustion. Decide if it is avoidance. One decision treated as real, owned without an escape clause drafted in the same breath. Advisors who profit from your indecision will always discover one more hallway. Walk through a door anyway.`,
